# Build-context ignore rules for the PCE PCB Viewer DEMO image (the same as production's).
#
# The Dockerfile is single-stage and does `COPY . .`, so anything left in the
# context is baked into the image the server runs from. Secrets and local state
# must not be in there — `guard security web-exposure` gates this.

# Secrets
.env
# Patterns are anchored at the context root, so the Deployment/*/.env files need their own line.
**/.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Version control and local agent/editor state
.git
.gitignore
.aimecca
.claude
.vscode
.idea

# Reinstalled inside the image by `npm ci`
node_modules

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# A demo stamp is written inside the demo image only. One left in the context must never reach
# production, where server.js would refuse to start without test mode.
demo-copy.stamp
